<p style="font-size:12px;color:#5b647a;line-height:1.6;margin:0;max-width:960px;">All figures are for The Life Link's fiscal year 2026 (July 1, 2025 – June 30, 2026) and come from the agency's Annual Quality Improvement Plan and Report. Behavioral health counts exclude people who received housing assistance only. Satisfaction scores are weighted averages of anonymous client surveys (n = 431) on a 1–5 scale. Demographic percentages exclude clients who did not report that information. Human trafficking program outcomes and New Mexico context come from The Life Link's Human Trafficking Outreach &amp; Aftercare Outcomes Reference (2015–2025), drawing on DOJ Office for Victims of Crime program evaluations and program service data; survivor contacts from 2022 onward include anonymous and hotline contacts. Survivor quotes are shared anonymously.</p>
